      "author": "Hollowmere team",
      "story": "Postmaster Walt Benning kept sorting after the Cordon stopped the outgoing mail, because people kept writing. He locked the front doors and left the box lobby open for anyone waiting on a letter. Six registered cartons from Cordon Medical for Dr. Asante at the clinic sat in the registry cage, unsigned for. When the two carriers came back off Rural Route 2 sick, he shut them in the loading dock and nailed the workroom door, bolted the dock from inside, and hung the cage key by his office door. Then something came through the boxes from the lobby side, and he went down into the basement with a lantern and never came back up the way he went.",
